{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Getting It Right", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A Convincing Argument", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe detailed facts about events or actions in work and social contexts, in written or spoken situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le18ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Wh-Clause in Exclamations", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use the wh-clause for exclamations. These sentences can show strong feelings.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "If you want to make an exclamatory sentence, you can use <span class=\"strong\">what</span> or <span class=\"strong\">how</span>. Follow the same structure as with the other wh-clauses. You can also use an exclamation mark at the end of these sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">It's wonderful <span class=\"strong\">how</span> lovely the weather is!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What</span> a beautiful baby!</span> (use of a/an with singular count nouns)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What</span> beautiful children!</span> (no article with plural count nouns)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use <span class=\"strong\">what</span> with plural and non-count nouns, or <span class=\"strong\">how</span>, it is sometimes difficult to decide whether it is an exclamation or a regular wh-clause. The background information or context is usually what helps you to decide.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">You don't know <span class=\"strong\">what</span> obstacles I've faced!<br/> You don't know <span class=\"strong\">what</span> the obstacles were that I faced.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I can't believe <span class=\"strong\">how</span> well she speaks!<br/> I can't believe <span class=\"strong\">how</span> she speaks so well.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I hope you all know what a special club this is!  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You'd never believe what problems you can avoid by using effective techniques of communication.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Past Continuous for Temporary Habitual Action", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use the Past Continuous or Past Progressive verb tense to talk about temporary repeated actions in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Not everything in life is permanent. If you want to talk about a habit in the past that was temporary, you can use the Past Continuous tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "How to form the Past Continuous:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\">form of <span class=\"italic\">be'</span>+ verb- ing</span></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">I<br/></span>  <div class=\\\"center_text\\\">He/ She/ it</span></span><br/><br/><div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">You<br/></span> <div class=\\\"center_text\\\">We<br/></span> <div class=\\\"center_text\\\">They</span></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<br/><div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">was (wasn't)<br/><br/><div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">were (weren't)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<br/><div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">eating\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Last year, I studied English in Canada for six months. I <span class=\"strong\">was speaking</span> in English for almost 8 hours a day with my friends. Also, I <span class=\"strong\">wasn't smoking</span> a lot since the cigarettes there were very expensive.</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I used to work in the legal system, so at that time, I was using arguments like the air we breathe. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My secret to writing convincing speeches was figuring out how you could use opinion and facts to help people, not to destroy them. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "analogy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a use of language that compares one thing to something else", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Take my example about arguments being like the air we breathe. This is an analogy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le18ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about how to make a good argument.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "familiar face", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone you know", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's nice to see so many familiar faces in the crowd.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le18ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "like the air we breathe", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very common; plentiful", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I used to work in the legal system, so at that time, I was using arguments like the air we breathe. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le18ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to have (no) merit ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to (not) deserve", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  An argument about economics or politics has no merit if it's not backed up with history and statistics demonstrating the case.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le18ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "valid ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "acceptable; logical; reasonable", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We all have equally valid opinions, but my argument is only superior to yours if I support it with facts. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le18ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be backed up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be supported", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Arguments need to be backed up with precise facts.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le18ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a list of the strategies for making a good argument that are discussed in this lesson.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, discuss other ways of making a good argument.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Go online. Find more strategies for making a good argument. Find at least 10 strategies.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 2-3 sentences summarizing each strategy.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your list to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I discuss strategies for making a good argument.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read about strategies for making a good argument.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a list describing each strategy.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le18ob03re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le18ob03re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn10le18ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "time": "0", "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn10le18ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "time": "100", "text": "It's nice to see so many familiar faces in the crowd. I hope you all know what a special club this is!  My name is Todd Jefferson, and tonight I'm going to talk to you about how to make a convincing argument.  I used to work in the legal system, so at that time, I was using arguments like the air we breathe.  Arguments are won not by having the best facts, but by expressing them in the best way.  You'd never believe what problems you can avoid by using effective techniques of communication.<br/>First, take my example about arguments being like the air we breathe. This is an analogy. It gives you a mental picture of words and ideas. It's amazing how effective analogies can be."}, {"image": "engenn10le18ob03re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "time": "45000", "text": "Secondly, facts do matter. As a lawyer, I was trying to find legal examples to support my case. In my view, an argument about economics or politics has no merit if it's not backed up with history and statistics. Otherwise, it's just an opinion. We all have equally valid opinions, but my argument is only superior to yours if I support it with facts. <br/>Thirdly, you should always be constructive.  I used to write speeches for an ambitious local politician. My secret to writing convincing speeches was figuring out how you could use opinion and facts to help people, not to destroy them."}, {"image": "engenn10le18ob03re2img03.jpg", "id": 3, "time": "88000", "text": "Finally, you have to strike an optimistic tone. Try to avoid negative thinking: \u201cI've had enough of this!\u201d Sometimes, you need to be courageous to find positive things to say. I maintain that there are many things to be positive about in the world."}]}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can express beliefs, opinions, and annoyance.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can report details, reasons, or results of events or actions.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can describe past habits. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Do you think you are convincing when you are trying to give your point of view? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What are some ways people can give convincing arguments?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": " Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "That makes a lot of sense!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "questions": []}, {"id": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " Todd Jefferson gives a speech about how to make a <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">convincing</span> argument.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}]}, {"content": [{"content": " Something that is <span class=\"italic\">\u201cconvincing\u201d</span> convinces you (or leads you) to do something or think in a certain way.", "type": "text", "tip_id": 0}], 